From 476ca75c9573c1a44033d13d7d05702e6a00fd4a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 19:02:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] hw: Undo and restore put back a kept version with its
 script paths

Why: the hardware-file store refuses any save whose [run_script] paths
differ from the file's. That is the owner's rule: script paths are set
over ssh, so nobody on the camera's network can point a button at a
script. But the same test also refused Undo, a History version and
restore=true whenever a path had changed in between, so a saved version
could not be put back. In Apertar 1.6.0 the Config page writes the whole
file, paths included.

What: the rule stays for a path nobody set over ssh. A save may bring
the script paths of a version Core kept (hardware-history, the last text
it wrote): those paths were on the camera before. The test compares the
paths themselves, not who the client says it is, so by=webui_undo with a
new path is still refused. README says where script paths are set.

Tested: check_core.sh both builds and the host tests pass. In --simulate
with a hardware file holding path1=a.sh: a browser save with a new path
is refused ("Script paths are changed over ssh, not here."); a save of
another key is written; after the file is edited outside Core to b.sh,
Undo to the earlier version is written and the file holds a.sh again; an
Undo that carries a path no kept version has is refused. Needs the
camera: nothing beyond this.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NEFc1w7Y8dcyiV489BiwMr
---
 README.md                            |  2 +-
 src/hardware/HardwareConfigStore.cpp | 15 +++++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 719b474..4d4e7a0 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -174,7 +174,7 @@ P2=capture
 
 These are mapping examples, not a complete hardware configuration. Use the correct section, pin numbering and wiring for your device. Grouped toggles flip independently; they do not force every option into the same state.
 
-The `run_script` action can run up to five configured scripts. Scripts run as the Core service user, without automatic administrator privileges. Only use scripts you trust.
+The `run_script` action can run up to five configured scripts. Scripts run as the Core service user, without automatic administrator privileges. Only use scripts you trust. The script paths in `[run_script]` are changed over ssh: the WebUI refuses a save that sets a new path, so nobody on the camera's network can point a button at a script. Undo, History and restore may put back a version the camera saved earlier, with the paths that version had.
 
 ## Boot Config (config.txt)
 
diff --git a/src/hardware/HardwareConfigStore.cpp b/src/hardware/HardwareConfigStore.cpp
index f91ad58..a0ef7ee 100644
--- a/src/hardware/HardwareConfigStore.cpp
+++ b/src/hardware/HardwareConfigStore.cpp
@@ -41,6 +41,17 @@ std::map<std::string, std::string> scriptPaths(const hwconf::Document &doc)
     return out;
 }
 
+// True when a version Core kept (the history, the last text it wrote) has exactly these script paths. Putting a
+// saved version back is not typing a path in the browser: its paths were set over ssh once.
+bool keptScriptPaths(const std::filesystem::path &notes, const std::map<std::string, std::string> &paths)
+{
+    std::error_code error;
+    for (const auto &entry : std::filesystem::directory_iterator(notes / "hardware-history", error))
+        if (scriptPaths(hwconf::parse(readTextFile(entry.path()))) == paths)
+            return true;
+    return scriptPaths(hwconf::parse(readTextFile(notes / "hardware-last-written.conf"))) == paths;
+}
+
 std::string timestamp(const char *format, std::time_t when)
 {
     std::tm local {};
@@ -327,8 +338,8 @@ StoreResult HardwareConfigStore::saveLocked(const std::string &base, const std::
         return result;
     }
 
-    const hwconf::Document nextDoc = hwconf::parse(next);
-    if (scriptPaths(nextDoc) != scriptPaths(currentDoc)) {
+    const auto nextPaths = scriptPaths(hwconf::parse(next));
+    if (nextPaths != scriptPaths(currentDoc) && !keptScriptPaths(notes_, nextPaths)) {
         result.code = "script_paths";
         result.error = "Script paths are changed over ssh, not here.";
         return result;
